what's going on guys this is rob and  today on our beyond omega level series  we're going to discuss gladiator who is  one of the many iterations of marvel  superman uh and you guys will find out  exactly just how close this guy is to  superman arguably he's the closest thing  that marvel has maybe with the exception  of hyperion but gladiator whose real  name is khalak was created by chris  claremont and dave cockrum and first  appeared in x-men number 107 in 1977.  now for a bit of interesting background  here each of the members of the shiar  imperial guard were created as homages  to the legion of superheroes of dc  comics and gladiator is a homage to  superman or superboy depending on who  you're talking about but his name being  kallark is literally a mashup of the  names khalel and clark and the name  gladiator is a nod to the novel of the  same name that serves as an inspiration  for the creation of superman now kallark  belongs to a race of aliens called the  strontiums who fall under the control of  the shiar empire but the species  possesses great inherent strength and  were trained as cadets in service of the  empire now kalark stood out among all of  his peers and was among a group of 10  elite recruits that would have their  power levels greatly enhanced after  completing a series of trials and so the  final test presented to the cadets  before being elevated to the title of  gladiator was to go back to their home  planet of strontia and kill the  strontian council of elders now of the  10 people only kallark proved his  devotion by having the willingness to  obey this command as he carried out the  killing of the beings who were  responsible for raising him and his  loyalty was ultimately rewarded as he  was elevated to gladiator status and  named praetor of the shia imperial guard  basically its leader devoted to  protecting the leader of the shia empire  so like i said earlier once he was  promoted to gladiator kellogg's power  level increased drastically and since  we've established that gladiator was a  creation or created as a homage to  superman to superboy it comes as no  surprise that his power set is virtually  identical so that means of course that  he has super strength and i feel like  glidator is often overlooked in terms of  how strong he actually is and that's  probably because he's been written  pretty inconsistently over the years but  when we look at what he's done it  becomes clear this guy is definitely one  of the strongest characters in marvel  comics and it makes sense that he was  part of the annihilators so for instance  when he hits ben grimm ben states it was  the hardest hit he had ever endured and  this was after he had squared off with  the incredible hulk on more than one  occasion in a battle with invisible  woman who's bonded with the unipower  which is the power that gives  individuals the power of captain  universe gladiator not only held his own  but the two of them caused a tsunami  that threatened to destroy california on  another occasion gladiator was engaged  in a test of strength with hyperion and  both of them exerted enough force to  pulverize a planet but most notably  gladiator was able to punch a planet  apart with only a couple of hits also  although we don't see it happen on panel  the living tribunal states that  gladiator is capable of removing planets  from their orbits and collapse stars  with his bare hands furthermore  gladiator's son kid gladiator remarks  that his father can crack moons with his  punches and tear black holes apart and  gladiator himself says that he's flown  through stars and can move planets at  will so we're talking about an  absolutely insane level of strength when  it comes to this guy now in addition to  his strength gladiator also has  superhuman durability having survived an  explosion that would have annihilated  half of the solar system and was  completely unfazed by a blast from  vulcan who himself is basically omega  level furthermore gladiator laughed when  he was hit with the nova flame from the  human torch and red sun that was 100  million miles wide without suffering any  ill effects another often overlooked  aspect of gladiator's power set is his  super speed in terms of his reflexes  he's caught around from a sniper rifle  and when it comes to pure speed he's  been able to outrun photons which are  basically particles of light which means  he can travel faster than the speed of  light in fact reed richards actually  observed that he traveled at 100 times  the speed of light when he approached  the earth and also covered a distance of  multiple light years in a matter of  seconds on top of that gladiator  possesses microvision which allows him  to count 10 billion micro sentinels in  jean grey's bloodstream in an instant  but the similarities to superman don't  stop there  he also possesses a form of x-ray vision  and heat vision with his heat vision  being hotter than a star and powerful  enough to destroy asteroids turn air  into plasma and cause molecules to  vibrate so quickly that they burn  galactus also much like superman  gladiator possesses a form of frost  breath that was capable of snuffing out  the flame of the human torch who at his  absolute peak is as hot as the sun now  with all that in mind it's obvious that  gladiator is at least omega level i mean  we know he can destroy planets and it's  said that he's able to collapse black  holes so there really shouldn't be much  debate as to whether gladiator belongs  in the omega or even beyond omega level  tier unfortunately like i said earlier  he's been the victim of extremely  inconsistent writing throughout his  numerous appearances and i think the  result of this inconsistent writing is  that many readers vastly underestimate  his power level just to give an example  of what i'm talking about here on the  one hand we have all these feats that  should speak for themselves as to how  powerful this guy is but then we have  other instances where he's knocked down  by gambit  or has a hard time overpowering colossus  but this is a problem that has played  comic book characters for years and as  readers inconsistent writing is  something we are just gonna have to  accept that there are going to be  instances when the bad guy or antagonist  is going to be hurt by a character they  logically should be able to easily  destroy because that's what the story  calls for and when gladiator runs into  the x-men the x-men are ultimately going  to win because the book is called x-men  it's not called gladiator but at the end  of the day we have seen what gladiator  can do and we've seen him give the  phoenix 5 a run for their money in  avengers vs x-men the phoenix force even  when divided among 5 hosts is one of the  most powerful forces in marvel comics so  the fact that gladiator can even  challenge them is impressive so despite  all the inconsistencies in writing i'm  comfortable in saying that based on his  feats gladiator is easily omega level  and could potentially be classified as a  beyond omega level threat but let me  know what you guys think down in the  comments section i'm really curious  because i'll be honest man people sleep  on gladiator this dude is just op but  we're going to bring this to an end  thank you all for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace
 

